    "title": "Tricia Cotham shares brief updates on social media following election to NC House",
    "text": "Tricia Cotham, a Republican member of the North Carolina State House representing the 105th district, posted a series of tweets between May 18 and May 20, 2026.\nOn May 18, Cotham wrote, “Happy Monday! https://t.co/DAnRRcutE2”. Two days later, on May 20, she posted another message: ” https://t.co/1FFZ6NzAiU”. Later that same day, she tweeted again: “Let’s go! https://t.co/TfrjycNbbL”.\nCotham was elected to the North Carolina State House in 2025 as a Republican to represent the state’s 105th House district. She succeeded Wesley Harris in this role.",
    "summary": "Tricia Cotham, a Republican member of the North Carolina State House representing the 105th district, posted a series of tweets between May 18 and May 20, 2026. On May 18, Cotham wrote, “Happy Monday! Two days later, on May 20, she posted another message: ” https://t.co/1FFZ6NzAiU”. Cotham was elected to the North Carolina State House in 2025 as a Republican to represent the state’s 105th House district. She succeeded Wesley Harris in this role.",
